The licence above covers the source in this repository. It does not cover the
payloads under `binaries/`, which are not the authors' to license:

  * `16476800119700000.zip` — partition images from Meta's Quest 1 firmware.
    Proprietary to Meta Platforms, Inc. Redistributed here only so the tool can
    write them back to the device they came from.
  * `ionstack`, `dev/ionstack-quest3` — third-party kernel exploit binaries,
    included with their author's permission and under whatever terms that
    author sets.

`bootctl_shim` is built from `native/bootctl_shim.c` in this repository and is
covered by the licence above. Its headers in `native/bc_min.h` are layouts
copied from AOSP (Apache-2.0).

Third-party code bundled into the built output:

  * LZMA-JS by Nathan Rugg, MIT licensed, taken from npm (`lzma`). It is
    imported normally; `vite.config.ts` only rewrites its trailing global
    assignment so it can be loaded as an ES module.
